## Computing and solving the error sets E and effect sets R of the bodies of a group (spec 7, 8,
## 9.4). Follows `body/errors.rs` and `body/effects.rs` of the reference type checker.
##
## After the types of a group are inferred, each expression's E is computed bottom-up: a call adds
## the callee function type's E, `fail e` the tag of e's type, `escape` removes the errors its arms
## fully catch. A body's E is contained in the declared E. Together with the inclusion constraints
## that unification collected, these are solved for the least solution, and every constraint is
## then checked.
##
## - If `sup` of a constraint `sub ⊆ sup` has a set variable, the elements of `sub` not in `sup`
##   become lower bounds of its first set variable, minus the effect tags of `sup`.
## - `escape` replaces a set variable with a fresh one whose solution excludes the caught tags.
## - A set variable in a negative position of a pending definition's type (the E of a function
##   parameter) with no bounds stays a variable, to be generalized; others take the least solution.
